{"w":2400,"lines":[{"y":0.04208994609117489,"h":0.014657317069460607,"x":0.087352233592197973,"t":"Test 3","c":1,"w":0.060246988932291676},{"x":0.40388349338119978,"w":0.19805825551350908,"h":0.015988371899566145,"t":"The steam car","c":1,"y":0.091569767519997902},{"x":0.17270199193622299,"y":0.12867112271676029,"w":0.66235402425130219,"h":0.019351065567349335,"c":1,"t":"The successes and failures of the Doble brothers and their steam cars"},{"h":0.021133361055843514,"t":"When primitive automobiles first began to appear in the 1800s, their engines were based","c":1,"y":0.16649177922019742,"w":0.76529129028320309,"x":0.12028952660083121},{"w":0.75753977457682287,"t":"on steam power. Steam had already enjoyed a long and successful career in the railways,","x":0.1318887954962393,"y":0.18456731990851871,"h":0.022765749637211563,"c":1},{"t":"so it was only natural that the technology evolved into a miniaturized version which was","w":0.75560409545898444,"h":0.021920272494402204,"c":1,"x":0.13191035479047003,"y":0.20380082489014506},{"t":"separate from the trains. But these early cars inherited steam's weaknesses along with its","y":0.22142087973785496,"w":0.75759063720703124,"x":0.13187970668009105,"c":1,"h":0.022958320546373034},{"c":1,"h":0.022451432843074715,"x":0.13191134729077494,"w":0.78475219726562506,"y":0.24114514005225907,"t":"strengths. The boilers had to be lit by hand, and they required about twenty minutes to build"},{"w":0.77503138224283852,"x":0.13384132782964797,"c":1,"t":"up pressure before they could be driven. Furthermore, their water reservoirs only lasted for","y":0.25992092511585696,"h":0.021894056849019128},{"w":0.765278065999349,"x":0.13191244509475097,"h":0.022437634572061826,"c":1,"t":"about thirty miles before needing replenishment. Despite such shortcomings, these newly","y":0.27749551171518216},{"c":1,"t":"designed self-propelled carriages offered quick transportation, and by the early 1900s it was","w":0.78475357055664074,"x":0.13383713905801822,"y":0.29617477528595182,"h":0.023985726662514084},{"t":"not uncommon to see such machines shuttling wealthy citizens around town.","y":0.31488144334766555,"c":1,"x":0.13182688377285842,"h":0.025244005149769988,"w":0.65863733927408852},{"y":0.35314674871457119,"w":0.68182601928710929,"h":0.021618379016531519,"x":0.13386337252719899,"c":1,"t":"But the glory days of steam cars were few. A new technology called the Internal"},{"t":"Combustion Engine soon appeared, which offered the ability to drive down the road just","y":0.37191653022602456,"x":0.13390492844777005,"w":0.75550577799479168,"h":0.02159831679870039,"c":1},{"h":0.019003115264797477,"t":"moments after starting up. At first, these noisy gasoline cars were unpopular because they","y":0.39096573195794149,"c":1,"w":0.76310679117838531,"x":0.13398058498574653},{"x":0.1338767200081577,"w":0.75557566324869785,"h":0.021330994460441621,"c":1,"t":"were more complicated to operate and they had difficult hand-crank starters, which were","y":0.40943351024571029},{"c":1,"x":0.13382833136450964,"w":0.76921808878580722,"y":0.42669400666812063,"t":"known to break arms when the engines backfired. But in 1912 General Motors introduced","h":0.021473078267225221},{"t":"the electric starter, and over the following few years steam power was gradually phased out.","h":0.024349481220185987,"y":0.44471786855366147,"w":0.78473200480143235,"c":1,"x":0.13381970783122293},{"h":0.024438835453021612,"x":0.13382690632228558,"c":1,"t":"Even as the market was declining, four brothers made one last effort to rekindle the","y":0.48137360965412701,"w":0.71295898437500005},{"w":0.78474548339843753,"h":0.023824802291727565,"c":1,"y":0.50134912274042798,"x":0.13191654575465217,"t":"technology. Between 1906 and 1909, while still attending high school, Abner Doble and his"},{"c":1,"h":0.021249111567702261,"y":0.52017512598629012,"t":"three brothers built their first steam car in their parents' basement. It comprised parts taken","w":0.77304890950520844,"x":0.13385284647679857},{"h":0.024889233550550061,"y":0.53764025565259743,"c":1,"x":0.13381674110978481,"t":"from a wrecked early steam car but reconfigured to drive an engine of their own design.","w":0.75176213582356777},{"h":0.021594250165042128,"y":0.55812937568808352,"w":0.78665924072265625,"c":1,"x":0.13579548628005075,"t":"Though it did not run well, the Doble brothers went on to build a second and third prototype"},{"y":0.57848837236417072,"h":0.01901941566823806,"c":1,"x":0.1339805867302557,"w":0.75728154500325529,"t":"in the following years. Though the Doble boys' third prototype, nicknamed the Model B,"},{"x":0.13372041142131064,"w":0.73260467529296869,"y":0.59222664234257794,"c":1,"t":"still lacked the convenience of an internal combustion engine, it drew the attention of","h":0.028564215449157881},{"x":0.13580421217325256,"w":0.77300415039062498,"c":1,"y":0.61415171375028688,"t":"automobile trade magazines due to its numerous improvements over previous steam cars. .","h":0.021591716540565464},{"y":0.63236776399472738,"w":0.78661295572916667,"t":"The Model B proved to be superior to gasoline automobiles in many ways. Its high-pressure","x":0.13582934954621143,"h":0.022340245707384243,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.78085215250651041,"t":"steam drove the engine pistons in virtual silence, in contrast to clattering gas engines which","y":0.65064702723876122,"x":0.13577489559825173,"h":0.023139430726428656},{"w":0.76730636596679691,"x":0.1357673179153151,"h":0.02498157536872081,"c":1,"y":0.66944688742353997,"t":"emitted the aroma of burned hydrocarbons. Perhaps most impressively, the Model B was"},{"y":0.68858918663605084,"w":0.79038416544596357,"c":1,"h":0.020903403736720505,"t":"amazingly swift. It could accelerate from zero to sixty miles per hour in just fifteen seconds,","x":0.13586204819066078},{"x":0.13578311988112679,"t":"a feat described as 'remarkable acceleration' by Automobile magazine in 1914.","y":0.70737743551002996,"w":0.67403345743815102,"h":0.022906829263562356,"c":1},{"t":"The following year Abner Doble drove the Model B from Massachusetts to Detroit in order","c":1,"y":0.74147674861469992,"w":0.78285558064778649,"x":0.13573291988792477,"h":0.02577678644768544},{"w":0.79051615397135422,"h":0.022619482735607099,"x":0.13581532501776053,"y":0.76405360436391112,"c":1,"t":"to seek investment in his automobile design, which he used to open the General Engineering"},{"h":0.020858182342624376,"c":1,"x":0.13780452907254745,"y":0.78313059832382825,"w":0.74381464640299466,"t":"Company. He and his brothers immediately began working on the Model C, which was"},{"t":"intended to expand upon the innovations of the Model B. The brothers added features such","w":0.7750319417317707,"y":0.80065972129952312,"h":0.022014333897290572,"x":0.13579924109866823,"c":1},{"h":0.022716954786829446,"y":0.81911095718579741,"t":"as a key-based ignition in the cabin, eliminating the need for the operator to manually","c":1,"x":0.1377246272900525,"w":0.73037206013997391},{"t":"ignite the boiler. With these enhancements, the Dobles'new car company promised a steam","x":0.1357914550412507,"y":0.83812571149768289,"h":0.023218352178175583,"w":0.78086441040039067,"c":1},{"h":0.021029339846792228,"y":0.8575865696478433,"c":1,"w":0.78466100056966148,"t":"vehicle which would provide all of the convenience of a gasoline car, but with much greater","x":0.13776900205657777},{"h":0.024200012824988404,"y":0.87477899396575132,"t":"speed, much simpler driving controls, and a virtually silent powerplant. By the following","x":0.13767832981567238,"c":1,"w":0.76149032592773425},{"y":0.89461116211991043,"w":0.76521601359049485,"h":0.022957247439945982,"t":"April, the General Engineering Company had received 5,390 deposits for Doble Detroits,","c":1,"x":0.13776928555895798},{"y":0.91557632393533595,"w":0.42135920206705729,"c":1,"t":"which were scheduled for delivery in early 1918.","x":0.13786409049559761,"h":0.017563210246718919},{"x":0.091262135177114539,"t":"66","h":0.014534883112922281,"y":0.95930232582483732,"w":0.027184467315673824,"c":1}],"h":3209}